# descent-vk brute_railgun: the brute with its shoulder railgun, as ONE mesh.
# For the level editor's preview and the level's placement proxy only. The game
# draws a brute_railgun as brute.obj plus railgun.obj, separately, because the
# gun can be shot off. This file is those two put together - brute.obj's
# vertices and faces unchanged, then railgun.obj's moved by the mount - so a
# change to either belongs in both.
# THIS MESH MUST STAY CLOSED. It is the brute's closed shell plus the gun's
# closed shells at RobotDef::railgunMount (2.2, 2.0, -1.1), sharing no vertex.
#
# -Z is forward. Wound counter-clockwise seen from outside; normals are not
# authored, the loader computes flat per-face normals.

